{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775393074-EkkmewRobD6cD632qETW","role":"assistant","created":1775393084,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the table with the gross federal obligations incurred outside the federal government as of March 31, 1988. This is Table FO-2.\n\nLooking at the table, I see columns including:\n- Personnel compensation\n- Personnel benefits\n- Benefits for former personnel\n- Transportation and transportation of persons\n- Transportation of things\n- Rent, communications, and utilities\n- Printing and reproduction\n- Other services\n- Supplies and materials\n\nThe question asks about \"service-related\" obligations. Looking at the categories, they appear to be:\n1. Personal services and benefits (personnel compensation, personnel benefits, benefits for former personnel)\n2. Contractual services and supplies (transportation, rent, printing, other services)\n3. Supplies and materials\n\nThe question asks what percentage are NOT \"service-related\" obligations. So I need to find the total and then subtract the service-related portion.\n\nLet me look at the totals:\n- Total Personnel compensation: 67998\n- Total Personnel benefits: 4737\n- Total Benefits for former personnel: 354\n- Total Transportation and transportation of persons: 2458\n- Total Transportation of things: 3415\n- Total Rent, communications, and utilities: 5919\n- Total Printing and reproduction: 169\n- Total Other services: 71362\n- Total Supplies and materials: 33399\n\nLet me calculate the total and figure out which categories are \"service-related\". Looking at typical government categorizations:\n- Personnel services (personnel compensation, benefits)\n- Contractual services (other services, transportation, rent, utilities, printing)\n- Supplies and materials\n\nActually, I think \"service-related\" would include:\n- Personnel compensation (pay for services)\n- Personnel benefits \n- Benefits for former personnel\n- Other services\n- Transportation of persons\n- Rent, communications, and utilities\n- Printing and reproduction\n\nAnd \"non-service\" would be:\n\n\n- Supplies and materials\n- Transportation of things (moving stuff, not people)\n\nI'm realizing the classification is more nuanced than initially thought. The terms suggest a specific interpretation of what constitutes a service versus a product. Transportation of things seems more like a logistical support function rather than a direct service. This means I'll need to carefully examine each category to determine its precise classification.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_2d745add47074c9cb1739b13","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '918,960p' /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1988_09.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
