{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775393090-bFo0GaGcnLQUmWQ94rpB","role":"assistant","created":1775393093,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So there's a chart on page 21 about \"Gross Federal obligations; gross Federal obligations incurred outside the Federal Government\". Let me look at the fraser.stlouisfed.org source URL to understand the chart better. The URL is https://fraser.stlouisfed.org/title/treasury-bulletin-407/september-1988-7054?page=37\n\nWait, that shows page 37 but refers to page 21 content. Let me look more carefully at the chart content. Let me also see if there's a visual chart representation somewhere.\n\nLooking at the tables I found:\n- Table FO-1: Gross obligations incurred within and outside the Federal Government by object class\n- Table FO-2: Gross obligations incurred outside the Federal Government by department or agency\n\nLet me look for FO-1 which might show object class categories:\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_84c037cecb29484faf17b7d4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"FO-1\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1988_09.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_d6687fc2-b5af-4150-8349-2bd525601090","role":"user","created":1775393093,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_84c037cecb29484faf17b7d4","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"76:| FFO-1.--Summary of fiscal operations | 11.0 |\n82:| FO-1.--Gross obligations incurred within and outside the Federal Government by object class | 18.0 |\n362:The first three Federal fiscal operations (FFO) tables are published quarterly and cover 5 years of data, estimates for 2 years, detail for 13 months, and fiscal year-to-date data. The tables are designed to provide a summary of data relating to Federal fiscal operations reported by Federal entities and disbursing officers, and daily reports from the Federal Reserve banks. These reports detail accounting transactions affecting receipts and outlays of the Federal Government and off-budget Federal entities, and their related effect on the assets and liabilities of the U.S. Government. Data used in the preparation of tables FFO-1, FFO-2, and FFO-3 is derived from the Monthly Treasury Statement of Receipts and Outlays of the United States Government.\n396:Table FFO-1.--Summary of Fiscal Operations\n505:Table FFO-1--Summary of Fiscal Operations\n813:Federal agencies often do business with one another; in doing so, the \"buying\" agency records obligations, and the \"performing agency records reimbursements. In table FO-1, obligations incurred within the Government are distinguished from those incurred outside the Government. Table FO-2 shows only those incurred outside.\n815:Table FO-1.--Gross Obligations Incurred Within and Outside the Federal Government by Object Class, as of Mar. 31, 1988","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"76:| FFO-1.--Summary of fiscal operations | 11.0 |\n82:| FO-1.--Gross obligations incurred within and outside the Federal Government by object class | 18.0 |\n362:The first three Federal fiscal operations (FFO) tables are published quarterly and cover 5 years of data, estimates for 2 years, detail for 13 months, and fiscal year-to-date data. The tables are designed to provide a summary of data relating to Federal fiscal operations reported by Federal entities and disbursing officers, and daily reports from the Federal Reserve banks. These reports detail accounting transactions affecting receipts and outlays of the Federal Government and off-budget Federal entities, and their related effect on the assets and liabilities of the U.S. Government. Data used in the preparation of tables FFO-1, FFO-2, and FFO-3 is derived from the Monthly Treasury Statement of Receipts and Outlays of the United States Government.\n396:Table FFO-1.--Summary of Fiscal Operations\n505:Table FFO-1--Summary of Fiscal Operations\n813:Federal agencies often do business with one another; in doing so, the \"buying\" agency records obligations, and the \"performing agency records reimbursements. In table FO-1, obligations incurred within the Government are distinguished from those incurred outside the Government. Table FO-2 shows only those incurred outside.\n815:Table FO-1.--Gross Obligations Incurred Within and Outside the Federal Government by Object Class, as of Mar. 31, 1988","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
